---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Crumbs from '../../../components/Crumbs.astro';
import FundraisingPlanner from '../../../components/FundraisingPlanner.astro';
import { fundraisingMethods, fundraisingSources } from '../../../data/fundraising.mjs';
import { url, issueUrl } from '../../../lib/site';
const steps = [
  ['Choose', 'Start with the mission, the audience and the time your team has.'],
  ['Test', 'Make a specific prediction and decide when to stop or revise.'],
  ['Follow up', 'Give each promised acknowledgment and update an owner.'],
  ['Learn', 'Keep the costs, limitations and disappointing results too.'],
];
const workflows = [
  { id: 'fundraising', title: 'Campaigns and gift references', text: 'Keep a campaign plan, pledges, externally confirmed gifts and acknowledgment records distinct.' },
  { id: 'projects', title: 'Owners and due dates', text: 'Create a task for each follow-up, assign its owner and review completion. Recurring successors are generated deliberately.' },
  { id: 'communications', title: 'Templates and communication choices', text: 'Review message text and purpose-specific consent. Keep provider suppression and delivery references beside the work.' },
  { id: 'evaluation', title: 'Evidence and learning', text: 'Write the question and method, record the findings and decide what the next campaign should change.' },
];
---
<Base title="Fundraising knowledge and practice" description="Sourced fundraising resources, ten practical method guides and a private campaign cost and follow-up planner. Connect the work to Charity OS.">
  <header class="page-head"><div class="wrap">
    <Crumbs items={[{ label: 'For charities', href: '/for-charities/' }, { label: 'Fundraising' }]} />
    <p class="eyebrow">A shared body of practice · Editorial draft</p>
    <h1>Make generosity<br />easier to sustain.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Ads, events and appeals are only part of fundraising. Connect the ask to the acknowledgment, the relationship and the next thing your team learns.</p>
    <nav class="hub-actions" aria-label="Start with fundraising"><a class="btn" href="#methods">Explore the methods</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#planner">Plan costs and follow-up</a><a href="#resources">Find research and peers</a></nav>
  </div></header>
  <div class="wrap">
    <ol class="practice-loop" aria-label="A proposed fundraising learning cycle">{steps.map(([title, text], i) => <li><span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">0{i + 1}</span><h2>{title}</h2><p>{text}</p></li>)}</ol>
    <section class="section-tight prose">
      <h2>There is already knowledge worth sharing</h2>
      <p>Fundraisers share benchmarks, experiments, training and professional discussions. The <a href="#resources">source guide below</a> explains what each can tell you. This hub adds a proposed route from reading to planning, follow-up and a reusable learning note. To find a peer community or founder program, explore the <a href={url('/for-charities/networks/')}>charity networks directory</a>.</p>
      <p>A benchmark describes its participants. An experiment tests an approach in a particular setting. Neither establishes the best method for every charity. The playbooks here are untested editorial starting points; adapt them and keep a record of what you find.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="section-tight" id="methods" aria-labelledby="methods-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Choose the job</p><h2 id="methods-title">Ten methods. One learning habit.</h2></div><p>Each guide covers preparation, full costs, measures, follow-up and an idea to test.</p></div>
      <div class="method-grid">{fundraisingMethods.map((method, i) => <a class="method-card" href={url(`/for-charities/fundraising/${method.id}/`)}><span class="method-number" aria-hidden="true">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><h3>{method.title}</h3><p>{method.summary}</p><span class="method-link">Read the playbook <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a>)}</div>
    </section>
    <section class="section-tight" id="planner" aria-labelledby="planner-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Put a plan beside the reading</p><h2 id="planner-title">Count the cost. Assign the follow-up.</h2>
      <p class="planner-intro">Compare cash and time costs, then prepare a campaign brief and calendar entries. Choose your own timing. The example intervals are a planning aid, not a tested email schedule. Your calendar controls its own notifications.</p>
      <FundraisingPlanner />
    </section>
    <section class="section-tight os-section" id="os" aria-labelledby="os-title">
      <div class="os-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Carry the work into Charity OS</p><h2 id="os-title">A task needs an owner.</h2><p>Use the shared workspace when several people need to keep the same commitments visible.</p></div><a class="btn" href="https://os.charitology.org">Open Charity OS <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <div class="workflow-grid">{workflows.map(workflow => <article><h3><a href={`https://os.charitology.org/#module/${workflow.id}`}>{workflow.title}</a></h3><p>{workflow.text}</p></article>)}</div>
      <p class="os-limit">Sign in and choose an organization to use these records. The planner does not import a campaign, create OS tasks or send donor emails. Record a delivery only after checking your sending provider. The OS’s reviewed templates and consent records do not themselves send a campaign.</p>
      <p><a href={url('/for-charities/os-plan/')}>Read the OS capabilities and implementation plan</a> · <a href={url('/for-charities/tools/')}>Compare external tools</a> · <a href={url('/for-charities/benefits/')}>Find nonprofit benefits</a></p>
    </section>
    <section class="section-tight" id="resources" aria-labelledby="resources-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Research, guidance and peers</p><h2 id="resources-title">Start from the original source.</h2></div><p>Source pages checked October 28, 2026 UTC. These summaries remain editorial drafts; access and programs can change.</p></div>
      <div class="resource-grid">{fundraisingSources.map(source => <article class="resource-card" id={`source-${source.id}`}><p class="eyebrow">{source.kind}</p><h3><a href={source.url}>{source.title} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h3><p>{source.summary}</p><p class="resource-limit"><strong>Read with care.</strong> {source.limits}</p></article>)}</div>
    </section>
    <section class="section-tight learning-note prose" id="share">
      <p class="eyebrow">Knowledge gets better when failures travel too</p><h2>Share a learning note.</h2>
      <p>Help another team understand what happened and whether it might apply to them. Keep donor identities, private figures and unpublished stories out of a public submission. Share only material you have permission to publish.</p>
      <ol><li><strong>Context:</strong> mission, location, campaign dates, audience and team capacity.</li><li><strong>Question:</strong> what you predicted, your comparison and the rule for stopping.</li><li><strong>Method:</strong> what changed, who was included and how results were attributed.</li><li><strong>Results:</strong> received funds, refunds, cash and time costs, follow-up and retention window. Leave missing values unknown.</li><li><strong>Limits:</strong> small samples, selection, seasonality, missing records and other plausible explanations.</li><li><strong>Next step:</strong> what you would repeat, change or stop. Include a source or an aggregate artifact others may inspect.</li></ol>
      <p><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://github.com/theguysaccount/charitology/issues/new?template=fundraising-learning.yml">Propose a public learning note</a> or <a href="https://github.com/theguysaccount/charitology/pulls">contribute a guide through a pull request</a>. Opening the form publishes nothing. Contributions need source and editorial review before being presented as findings.</p>
    </section>
    <aside class="section-tight prose"><h2>Keep the mission in view</h2><p>Money raised is an input to the work. It does not establish what changed for people or why. Review whether a campaign’s messages, restrictions and workload support the mission. Ask whose voice is missing from its story.</p><p>Fundraising acts on the signals and channels of charity. The work it supports may offer relief, repair, prevention, structure or source-level change. <a href={url('/method/')}>Depth describes the work; every level is needed.</a></p><p><a href={issueUrl('correction', 'Fundraising hub correction', 'https://charitology.org/for-charities/fundraising/')}>Correct a source or challenge this approach</a>.</p></aside>
  </div>
</Base>
<style>
  h1{max-width:15ch}.hub-actions{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:1.6rem}.practice-loop{list-style:none;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));padding:0;margin:0 0 1rem;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;background:var(--surface)}.practice-loop li{padding:1.4rem;border-right:1px solid var(--rule);min-width:0}.practice-loop li:last-child{border-right:0}.practice-loop h2{font-size:1.5rem;margin:.4rem 0}.practice-loop p{font-size:1rem;color:var(--ink-2);margin:0}.step-number,.method-number{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.8rem;color:var(--ink-3)}.section-heading{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:end;gap:2rem;margin-bottom:1.4rem}.section-heading h2{margin-bottom:0}.section-heading>p{max-width:33ch;color:var(--ink-2);margin:0}.method-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.method-card{padding:1.5rem;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:var(--radius);text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-width:0}.method-card:hover{border-color:var(--accent)}.method-card h3{font-size:1.5rem;margin:.5rem 0}.method-card p{color:var(--ink-2);margin:0 0 1rem}.method-link{font-family:var(--font-sans);font-size:.9rem;color:var(--accent);margin-top:auto}.planner-intro{max-width:70ch}.os-section{border-block:1px solid var(--rule);padding-block:2.5rem}.os-heading{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:2rem}.os-heading p{max-width:60ch}.os-heading h2{margin-bottom:.7rem}.workflow-grid,.resource-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.4rem}.workflow-grid article{padding-block:.6rem}.workflow-grid h3{font-size:1.2rem}.workflow-grid p,.os-limit{color:var(--ink-2)}.os-limit{font-size:.95rem;max-width:85ch}.resource-card{border-top:2px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0;min-width:0}.resource-card h3{font-size:1.3rem}.resource-limit{font-size:.95rem;color:var(--ink-2)}.learning-note{border-block:1px solid var(--rule);padding-block:2rem}section,aside{scroll-margin-top:5rem}a{overflow-wrap:anywhere}@media(max-width:700px){.practice-loop{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.practice-loop li:nth-child(2){border-right:0}.practice-loop li:nth-child(-n+2){border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}.section-heading,.os-heading{display:block}.section-heading>p{max-width:none;margin-top:1rem}.method-grid,.resource-grid,.workflow-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.hub-actions{align-items:flex-start}.os-heading>.btn{margin-bottom:1rem}}@media print{.hub-actions{display:none}.method-grid,.resource-grid,.workflow-grid{display:block}.method-card,.resource-card{break-inside:avoid}}
</style>
